cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DAIOE: Dynamic AI Occupational Exposure"
message: "If you use DAIOE, please cite both this release and the paper below."
type: dataset
# Authors are the paper's eleven, in the paper's order (alphabetical by surname).
#
# OWED BEFORE PUBLISHING, and it cannot be filled in from here:
#   1. An ORCID for every person. Collect them; do not look them up. A wrong ORCID
#      credits a stranger in a permanent record.
#   2. Affiliations for the eight left blank. Only Görg, Javed and Lodefalk carry a
#      verified affiliation in the manuscript; the others are anonymised placeholders
#      there, so they are omitted here rather than guessed.
# Zenodo also supports `contributors` with DataCite roles (DataCurator, Researcher,
# ProjectLeader) if the group later wants to distinguish who built the measure from
# who contributed to the work around it.
authors:
  - family-names: Engberg
    given-names: Erik
  - family-names: Görg
    given-names: Holger
    affiliation: "Kiel Institute for the World Economy"
  - family-names: Hellsten
    given-names: Mark
  - family-names: Javed
    given-names: Farrukh
    affiliation: "Department of Statistics, Lund University"
  - family-names: Lodefalk
    given-names: Magnus
    affiliation: "Örebro University; Ratio Institute; Global Labor Organization"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0149-9598"
  - family-names: Längkvist
    given-names: Martin
  - family-names: Monteiro
    given-names: Natália
  - family-names: Kyvik Nordås
    given-names: Hildegunn
  - family-names: Pulito
    given-names: Giuseppe
  - family-names: Schroeder
    given-names: Sarah
  - family-names: Tang
    given-names: Aili
abstract: >-
  DAIOE translates measured performance gains on public AI benchmarks into
  occupation-year exposure scores, separately for nine capability subdomains and a
  generative-AI composite. Unlike static exposure indices it varies over time as well
  as across occupations, so the timing of capability arrival is observable and
  testable. Released with the full construction pipeline, its tests, and the vintage
  gates that keep the frozen publication index separate from later updates.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - occupational exposure
  - labour economics
  - task-based framework
  - technological change
  - O*NET
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Magnus-L/daioe-pipeline"
# --- COMPLETE THESE THREE AT RELEASE -----------------------------------------
# Zenodo can reserve a DOI before publishing: create the deposition, click
# "Reserve DOI", paste it here, then tag and publish so the record and the file
# agree. Use the CONCEPT DOI (the one that always resolves to the latest
# version), not the version DOI.
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "RESERVE-ON-ZENODO-BEFORE-PUBLISHING"
date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD"
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
references:
  - type: article
    title: "AI Unboxed: Capability Arrival and the Clerical Decline"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lodefalk
        given-names: Magnus
    notes: "Working paper; replace with the published reference at acceptance."
notes: >-
  VINTAGES ARE SEPARATE OBJECTS. The frozen 2010-2023 index underlies the published
  estimates; the 2024 refresh, the SOC2018 build and the 2025-onward vintage are
  distinct and are not interchangeable with it. Cite the vintage you used, not the
  repository as a whole. Code is MIT (see LICENSE); the scores are CC BY 4.0 (see
  LICENSE-DATA).
